<title>UK: Eight bootleggers jailed for UK customs fraud.</title>
<headline>Eight bootleggers jailed for UK customs fraud.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British judge on Wednesday sentenced eight men to a total of 25-1/2 years in prison for defrauding customs of 6.5 million pounds ($10.6 million) of tax on beer, wine and spirits.</p>
<p>Judge Chris Hodson sentenced the West Midlands men for bootlegging alcohol transported between Belgium and Britain, HM Customs and Excise said in a statement.</p>
<p>($ = 0.612 British Pounds)</p>
</text>
